```text
10. controller class + threading server
    swap base class: ThreadingHTTPServer (stdlib, same module) so concurrent requests work
    (streaming no longer blocks keyboard/ingest)

    reshape _Handler into a named Controller that:
      - holds service refs in __init__
      - one method per endpoint, decorated with @GET / @POST
      - methods return (status, content_type, body) tuples
      - server base does: parse path → lookup ROUTES dict → call method → write response
      - fallback: unmatched GET → static file serve (super().do_GET)
      - query params / body passed as args to the method
    - proxy endpoints (gpu box) return (status, content_type, bytes) — same tuple shape, just bytes
    - no pip deps, stays stdlib http.server under the hood

    supersmall skeleton:

    ROUTES: dict[tuple[str, str], Callable] = {}

    def GET(path):
        def deco(fn):
            ROUTES[("GET", path)] = fn
            return fn
        return deco

    def POST(path):
        def deco(fn):
            ROUTES[("POST", path)] = fn
            return fn
        return deco

    class ClankController:
        def __init__(self, ingestion, kb_service, prompt_service, gpu_box_url):
            self.ingestion = ingestion
            self.kb_service = kb_service
            self.prompt_service = prompt_service
            self.gpu_box_url = gpu_box_url

        @GET("/api/boot")
        def boot(self) -> tuple[int, str, str]: ...

        @GET("/api/char")
        def char(self, params: dict) -> tuple[int, str, dict]: ...

        @POST("/api/ingest")
        def ingest(self, body: str) -> tuple[int, str, dict]: ...

        @POST("/v1/chat/completions")
        def proxy_chat(self, body: bytes, headers: dict) -> tuple[int, str, bytes]: ...
        # same for /api/desktop-mode, /api/inference-mode

    class Server(ThreadingHTTPServer):
        # ~20 lines: parse, lookup, call, write, static fallback
```
